# Normalize line endings.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows can produce CRLF working-tree copies of
# LF-committed files. Git then reports every one of them as modified while the
# content is byte-identical, which buries real edits in noise and makes
# `make format-check` fail on a fresh clone. It has already cost time here: a
# working tree once showed 159 modified files, none of which contained a single
# content change.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores text as LF and checks it out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be normalized -- doing so corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
